{{page-title "Transitions"}}

{{!-- transition basics --}}
<div class="layout__section">
  <div class="layout__header">
    <div class="layout__container">
      <code>transition</code> Basics
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="layout__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        Manipulate CSS properties
      </div>

      <div class="section__description">
        <p>
          The CSS <code>transition</code> property allows you to change property values smoothly over a specified
          duration. It is useful for creating animations and making your web pages more interactive.
        </p>
        <p>
          <b>Transition Property</b>: Specifies the CSS property you want to animate.
        </p>
        <p>
          <b>Duration</b>: Specifies how long the transition should take.
        </p>
        <p>
          <b>Timing Function</b>: Specifies the speed curve of the transition (e.g., ease, linear, ease-in, ease-out).
        </p>
        <p>
          <b>Delay</b>: Specifies a delay before the transition starts (optional).
        </p>

        <br>

        <p>
          On the controls below, you can update the <code>background-color</code> property of Box A. Notice how the
          color changes with a transition instead of immediately changing. This is the effect of the transition
          <code>transition: background-color 1s linear;</code>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="section__body">
        <div class="demo-container">
          <div class="demo-item" style="width: 500px;">
            <div class="demo-item demo-item--base">
              <div
                class="demo-item demo-item--bg-a"
                style="width: 100%; height: 50%; padding: 16px; transition: background-color 1s linear; background: {{this.backgroundColor}}"
              >
                Box A
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="section__controls">
        <div class="section__controls__title">
          Controls
        </div>

        <div class="section__controls__input">
          <label for="color-1">
            Update <code>background color</code> from Box A

            <input
              id="color-1"
              type="color"
              value={{this.backgroundColor}}
              {{on 'input' this.updateBackgroundColor}}
            >
          </label>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{{!-- end transition basics --}}

{{!-- transition properties --}}
<div class="layout__section">
  <div class="layout__header">
    <div class="layout__container">
      Not all properties can be part of <code>transition</code>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="layout__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        Transition has limitations
      </div>

      <div class="section__description">
        <p>
          Not all CSS properties can be transitioned. Only properties that have an identifiable halfway point can be
          transitioned. For example, you can transition <code>width</code> but not <code>display</code>.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <b>display</b>: This property cannot be transitioned because it does not have intermediate states.
          </li>

          <li>
            <b>visibility</b>: Similar to display, it does not have intermediate states.
          </li>

          <li>
            <b>position</b>: Properties like static, relative, absolute, and fixed cannot be transitioned.
          </li>

          <li>
            <b>float</b>: This property does not support transitions.
          </li>

          <li>
            <b>height</b>: This property is transitionable, but it requires both defined initial and final values.
            It cannot be transitioned if it uses the <code>auto</code> value.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{{!-- end variable basics --}}

{{!-- advanced transitions --}}
<div class="layout__section">
  <div class="layout__header">
    <div class="layout__container">
      Complex <code>transition</code>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="layout__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        Transition everything!
      </div>

      <div class="section__description">
        <p>
          You can transition multiple properties at a time, with different times, delays, and timing functions.
        </p>
        <p>
          <code>transition: background-color 1s linear, border-color .2s ease, transform .5s ease;</code>
        </p>
        <p>
          The example above defines a transition that will update both <code>background-color</code> and
          <code>border-color</code> properties. The <code>background-color</code> will transition in 0.2 seconds with
          an ease timing function, while the <code>border-color</code> will transition in 0.5 seconds with a linear
          timing function.
        </p>
        <p>
          This means that you can create complex animations by transitioning multiple properties at once, potentially
          creating any effect you might need. This is specially useful on <code>:hover</code> transitions when more than
          a single property needs to change.
        </p>

        <br>

        <p>
          On the controls below, you can change the values of background-color, border-color and transform with
          different timings and animation functions. Inspect the code to see the <code>transition.</code>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="section__body">
        <div class="demo-container">
          <div class="demo-item" style="width: 500px;">
            <div class="demo-item demo-item--base">
              <div
                class="demo-item demo-item--bg-a"
                style="
                  position: relative;
                  width: 100%;
                  height: 50%;
                  padding: 16px;
                  border: 4px solid black;
                  z-index: 10;
                  transition: background-color 1s linear, border-color .2s ease, transform .5s ease;
                  {{this.transitionExample}}
                  "
              >
                Box B
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="section__controls">
        <div class="section__controls__title">
          Controls
        </div>

        <div class="section__controls__input">
          <button class="section__button" type="button" {{on 'click' this.toggleTransitionExample}}>
            Toggle Transition
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
{{!-- end advanced transitions --}}